---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Glossary"
	description="A living dictionary of terms in AI, NLP, and Speech."
	pubDate={new Date()}
>
	<p>
		The field of artificial intelligence is full of jargon. This is a living document defining key terms used across Neural Ground Truth posts.
	</p>

	<dl>
		<dt id="attention"><strong>Attention Mechanism</strong></dt>
		<dd>A technique that allows models to dynamically focus on different parts of an input sequence when processing data, solving the bottleneck problem in traditional sequence-to-sequence models.</dd>

		<dt id="kv-cache"><strong>KV-Cache</strong></dt>
		<dd>An optimization technique used during transformer inference to store previously computed Key and Value tensors, avoiding redundant calculations for past tokens.</dd>

		<dt id="low-resource"><strong>Low-Resource Language</strong></dt>
		<dd>A language that lacks large, high-quality digital datasets (text or audio) necessary for training modern machine learning models (e.g., Kinyarwanda, Fon, Ewe).</dd>
	</dl>

	<style>
		dt {
			font-size: 1.2em;
			margin-top: 1.5em;
			color: var(--accent);
		}
		dd {
			margin-left: 0;
			margin-top: 0.5em;
			padding-left: 1em;
			border-left: 2px solid var(--line);
			color: var(--ink-dim);
		}
	</style>
</Layout>
